{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"algebraicConnectivity","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"normalized","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = false, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = 1e-8, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? = nil) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV","text":"NoConvergence","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sz","text":"BinaryInteger","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full reorthogonalization, the null space projected"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, from a fixed start vector: on σI − L (σ twice the largest weighted degree; 2I − N with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"normalized"},{"type":"text","text":") while σ\/λ₂ is moderate, else on L⁺ by shift-invert, each product a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conjugate-gradient solve with L grounded at the vertex of largest degree. A Ritz pair is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accepted when its residual is at most "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance"},{"type":"text","text":" · λ₂, so λ₂ is relative to itself however"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the weights spread; the value is then the vector’s Rayleigh quotient, a sum over edges. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dense solver below 64 vertices. O((n + m) · products) time; 31 n "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s (34 n from 5,000"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices, for the polynomial filter), and on the shift-invert path O(n + m) more for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"solver."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position; a weight of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"0 is no edge.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"At least two vertices, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance > 0"},{"type":"text","text":". Every weight is finite and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nonnegative, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":", when given, is at least 1."}]}],"style":"note","name":"Precondition","type":"aside"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"NoConvergence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when the Lanczos run on L⁺ spends ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" matrix–vector","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"products (1,000 when nil) without converging, with the products spent and the Ritz","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"residual relative to 1\/λ₂. The run on σI − L that may come first hands over to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shift-invert rather than throwing, after 4,000 + 20√n products or ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whichever is smaller. Each shift-invert product is a conjugate-gradient solve that throws,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with its own iterations and relative residual, after 20,000 + 2n. Below 64 vertices the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dense solver answers and ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is unused. Only a tolerance below rounding has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reached the default limits in the measurements.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","name":"Throws","type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/algebraicconnectivity(weight:normalized:tolerance:maxiterations:)-8c3i6"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGra